Teach the fork's KV host to run without hugepages, and on a CPU it has.

test/nvmf/kv/kv_host.c is driven upstream by kv_vfio_user.sh, which runs inside
SPDK's own test environment where scripts/setup.sh has already reserved
hugepages. A container gets none unless it is privileged or /dev/hugepages is
mounted with pages reserved -- the same case entrypoint.sh's --no-huge fallback
exists for -- and kv_host takes no EAL arguments, so it dies at DPDK init
before it ever reaches the vfio-user socket.

The core mask is the same shape of problem as the hugepages: kv_host takes no
EAL arguments, so it uses SPDK's default mask of 0x1 and dies at DPDK init
wherever CPU 0 is outside the process's affinity. That is every Slurm
allocation that was not given core 0, and it is why this image was the one
target in the repo that could not build on a compute node.

Driven by environment variables rather than new argv options: argv is
positional in kv_host (<socket-dir> [reject|allow|rados-exec]) and adding a
flag there would diverge from the fork's own driver scripts. With the variable
unset the binary behaves exactly as it does upstream, so this cannot change
what the fork's tests exercise.

Retire this patch when the fork grows a --no-huge of its own; `git apply` fails
loudly if the context moves, which is the signal to come back here.

--- a/test/nvmf/kv/kv_host.c
+++ b/test/nvmf/kv/kv_host.c
@@ -193,6 +193,23 @@
 	opts.opts_size = sizeof(opts);
 	spdk_env_opts_init(&opts);
 	opts.name = "kv_host";
+	/* batesste-ci-images: no hugepages in a plain container. */
+	if (getenv("KV_HOST_NO_HUGE") != NULL) {
+		const char *mem_size = getenv("KV_HOST_MEM_SIZE");
+		int mem_mib = mem_size != NULL ? spdk_strtol(mem_size, 10) : -1;
+
+		opts.no_huge = true;
+		opts.mem_size = mem_mib > 0 ? mem_mib : 256;
+	}
+
+	/* batesste-ci-images: the default core mask is 0x1, and CPU 0 is not
+	 * ours to use under a constrained cpuset -- DPDK then fails startup
+	 * with "Cannot set affinity" rather than falling back to a CPU it has.
+	 */
+	if (getenv("KV_HOST_CPUMASK") != NULL) {
+		opts.core_mask = getenv("KV_HOST_CPUMASK");
+	}
+
 	if (spdk_env_init(&opts) < 0) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "Unable to initialize SPDK env\n");
 		return 1;
